---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const article = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'Article',
  headline: 'Turkey e-Visa from Pakistan — Complete Guide',
  author: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'VisaPath.pk' },
  publisher: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'VisaPath.pk' },
  datePublished: '2026-10-24',
};

const faq = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'FAQPage',
  mainEntity: [
    { '@type': 'Question', name: 'Can Pakistanis get Turkey e-Visa?',
      acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: 'Yes, but with conditions. Pakistani passport holders can get Turkey e-Visa only if they hold a valid Schengen, UK, US, or Ireland visa or residence permit.' } },
    { '@type': 'Question', name: 'How long is Turkey e-Visa valid?',
      acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: 'Turkey e-Visa is valid for 180 days from issue date, allowing a single entry and stay of up to 30 days.' } },
    { '@type': 'Question', name: 'What if I don\'t have Schengen or UK visa?',
      acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: 'Without a qualifying visa, Pakistani passport holders must apply for a Turkey sticker visa at the Turkish Embassy in Islamabad or Consulate in Karachi.' } },
  ],
};
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Turkey e-Visa from Pakistan — Complete 2026 Guide"
  description="How Pakistanis get Turkey e-Visa with Schengen, UK, or US visa. Alternative sticker visa process. Documents, fees, and tourist tips."
  schema={[article, faq]}
>
  <article class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 py-10">
    <nav class="text-sm text-gray-500 mb-4">
      <a href="/" class="hover:text-brand-600">Home</a> ›
      <a href="/guides/" class="hover:text-brand-600">Guides</a> ›
      <span>Turkey e-Visa</span>
    </nav>

    <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold mb-4">Turkey e-Visa from Pakistan — Complete Guide</h1>
    <p class="text-gray-500 text-sm mb-8">Last updated: October 2026 · 8 minute read</p>

    <section class="prose max-w-none">
      <p class="lead text-lg">
        Turkey is one of the most popular travel destinations for Pakistanis — Istanbul, Antalya, Cappadocia, and the Turkish Riviera attract tens of thousands annually. However, Pakistani passport holders need a visa before travel, and the easy e-Visa route has a specific condition.
      </p>

      <h2>Turkey e-Visa — Conditional for Pakistanis</h2>
      <p>
        As of 2026, Pakistani passport holders can apply for the online Turkey e-Visa <strong>only if they hold a valid visa or residence permit</strong> from one of the following:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Schengen Area country</li>
        <li>United Kingdom</li>
        <li>United States</li>
        <li>Republic of Ireland</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        The visa/residence permit must be valid at the time of your Turkey entry.
      </p>

      <h2>Who Qualifies for e-Visa</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Hold a Pakistani passport valid 6+ months beyond arrival</li>
        <li>Have a valid Schengen, UK, US, or Ireland visa (any type — tourist, student, work, residence)</li>
        <li>Travel for tourism or commerce only (not work)</li>
        <li>Stay no more than 30 days per entry</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>e-Visa Details</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Validity:</strong> 180 days from issue</li>
        <li><strong>Stay allowed:</strong> up to 30 days per entry</li>
        <li><strong>Entries:</strong> single entry</li>
        <li><strong>Fee:</strong> approximately $60 USD (via online payment)</li>
        <li><strong>Processing time:</strong> minutes to 24 hours</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>How to Apply Online</h2>
      <ol>
        <li>Visit the official <code>evisa.gov.tr</code> (beware of imitation sites that charge extra)</li>
        <li>Select nationality: Pakistan</li>
        <li>Select travel document: Ordinary Passport</li>
        <li>Confirm you hold a qualifying visa/residence permit</li>
        <li>Enter travel date</li>
        <li>Fill in passport details, address, email</li>
        <li>Pay fee by credit/debit card</li>
        <li>Receive e-Visa PDF by email</li>
        <li>Print and carry on arrival</li>
      </ol>

      <h2>Documents at Entry</h2>
      <p>At Turkish immigration, you may be asked to show:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Printed e-Visa</li>
        <li>Valid passport</li>
        <li>Qualifying Schengen/UK/US/Ireland visa or residence card</li>
        <li>Return or onward ticket</li>
        <li>Hotel reservation or address</li>
        <li>Proof of sufficient funds ($50 USD per day minimum)</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>If You Don't Have a Qualifying Visa — Sticker Visa</h2>
      <p>
        If you don't hold any of the qualifying visas, you need to apply for a traditional sticker visa at:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Turkish Embassy, Islamabad</strong></li>
        <li><strong>Turkish Consulate, Karachi</strong></li>
      </ul>

      <h3>Sticker Visa Process</h3>
      <ol>
        <li>Book appointment online via consulate website</li>
        <li>Complete application form</li>
        <li>Attend in person with documents</li>
        <li>Pay visa fee (approximately $80 USD)</li>
        <li>Submit biometrics if required</li>
        <li>Processing: 15 working days or more</li>
      </ol>

      <h3>Sticker Visa Documents</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>Passport valid 6+ months with 2 blank pages</li>
        <li>Application form</li>
        <li>2 biometric photos</li>
        <li>Round-trip flight reservation</li>
        <li>Hotel bookings for entire stay</li>
        <li>Travel insurance (€30,000 coverage)</li>
        <li>Bank statement — last 3 months</li>
        <li>Employment letter + salary slips</li>
        <li>Business documents (if self-employed)</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Common Issues</h2>
      <h3>e-Visa Issued Despite Not Qualifying</h3>
      <p>
        The e-Visa system doesn't verify your Schengen/UK/US visa at application. You can accidentally get an approved e-Visa without a qualifying visa. However, at Turkish immigration, if you cannot show one, you'll be denied entry and returned.
      </p>

      <h3>Expired Qualifying Visa</h3>
      <p>
        Your Schengen/UK/US/Ireland visa must be valid <strong>on the day of entry to Turkey</strong>, not just when you applied for the e-Visa. If it expires before your Turkey trip, the e-Visa is invalid.
      </p>

      <h3>Residence Permits Count</h3>
      <p>
        A Pakistani resident of UK, Schengen, or US with a valid residence permit (BRP, Carte de Séjour, Green Card, etc.) qualifies — residence permit works just like a visa for this purpose.
      </p>

      <h2>Travel Tips</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Istanbul:</strong> most Pakistani flights arrive here; stay in Sultanahmet (historic) or Taksim (modern)</li>
        <li><strong>Cappadocia:</strong> hot air balloons, cave hotels — book 2+ months ahead</li>
        <li><strong>Antalya:</strong> beach resorts, Mediterranean coast</li>
        <li><strong>Bodrum/Fethiye:</strong> upscale coastal escapes</li>
        <li><strong>Trabzon/Uzungöl:</strong> Black Sea region, popular with Pakistani travellers</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>Visa-Free Through Turkey to Other Countries</h3>
      <p>
        Turkey is often a connection for Pakistani travellers heading to Europe or Asia. Transit through Istanbul airport (IST or SAW) doesn't require a visa if you stay in the transit area.
      </p>

      <h2>Related Resources</h2>
      <p>
        <a href="/tools/passport-validity-checker/">Passport Validity Checker</a> ·
        <a href="/tools/visa-fee-calculator/">Fee Calculator</a> ·
        <a href="/guides/schengen-visa-pakistanis/">Schengen Visa Guide</a>
      </p>
    </section>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
